## TypeScript End User API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to be intuitive,  flexible, and robust for controlling 3D camera animations in TypeScript, balancing ease of use with powerful customization options.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub managing camera behavior. Instances represent individual cameras within your scene.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(target: THREE.Object3D, initialPosition: Vector3, FOV: number = 75) {
           this.target = target; // Object the camera orbits/follows
           this.position = initialPosition.clone(); // Initial camera location
           this.fov = FOV; // Field of View (adjustable)
           // ... internal state & methods (interpolation, easing, etc.)
       }

       // Animation Methods (Fluent Interface)
       animateTo(destination: Vector3, duration: number, easing = 'easeOutQuad'): this {
           this.queueAnimation({ type: 'moveTo', target: destination, duration, easing });
           return this; // Chainable for multiple actions
       }

       orbitAround(axis: 'X' | 'Y' | 'Z', radius: number, duration: number, rotationsPerSecond: number = 1, easing = 'linear'): this {
           this.queueAnimation({ type: 'orbit', axis, radius, duration, rotationsPerSecond, easing });
           return this;
       }

       zoom(factor: number, duration: number, easing = 'easeInOutExpo'): this {
           this.queueAnimation({ type: 'zoom', factor, duration, easing });
           return this;
       }

       // Advanced Control
       setLookAt(targetPoint: Vector3, upVector?: Vector3, duration?: number, easing?: string): this {
           // Directly sets camera lookAt with optional animation
           // ... implementation 
           return this;
       }

       // Playback & Management
       playAnimations(): void;
       pauseAnimations(): void;
       clearQueue(): void;
       getAnimationProgress(): number; //  0-1 progress of active animations

       private queueAnimation(params: AnimationParams): void; // Internal handling
   }
   ```

